 {"id": "PEDS-U270", "ch": 32, "n": 4, "title": "TOF — Cyanotic Spell & Management", "sec": "Cyanotic spell · p143", "qs": ["PEDS-C32-036", "PEDS-C32-037", "PEDS-C32-038", "PEDS-C32-039", "PEDS-C32-040", "PEDS-C32-041", "PEDS-C32-042", "PEDS-C32-043", "PEDS-C32-044", "PEDS-C32-045", "PEDS-C32-046", "PEDS-C32-047", "PEDS-C32-048", "PEDS-C32-049", "PEDS-C32-050", "PEDS-C32-051", "PEDS-C32-052", "PEDS-C32-053"], "guide": "Cyanotic spell: ↑ severity of cyanosis; disappearance of shunt murmur = surest sign of TOF. Cycle: infundibular spasm (narrowing) → worsening hypoxia → lactic acidosis → stimulation of respiratory centre → hyperventilation → ↑ venous return → more spasm. Management: O2, sodium bicarbonate, morphine (depress respiratory centre), β-blockers, squatting (older children)/knee-to-chest (infants) → femoral artery compression; α-agonist (phenylephrine) → ↑ SVR (aorta) → ↑ afterload for LV → ↓↓ RV→LV flow → ↓ cyanosis."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U271", "ch": 32, "n": 5, "title": "TOF — Surgical Treatment", "sec": "TOF surgery · p144", "qs": ["PEDS-C32-054", "PEDS-C32-055", "PEDS-C32-056", "PEDS-C32-057", "PEDS-C32-058", "PEDS-C32-059", "PEDS-C32-060", "PEDS-C32-061", "PEDS-C32-062", "PEDS-C32-063", "PEDS-C32-064"], "guide": "Definitive: VSD repair + correction of stenosis (performed < 3 months). Palliative shunt surgery → improve pulmonary blood flow → improve cyanosis: in delayed presentations or C/I to definitive surgery; method — shunting systemic artery to pulmonary artery: classic Blalock-Taussig (B-T) with subclavian artery; modified B-T (artificial conduit, m/c); Waterston with ascending aorta; Potts with descending aorta."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U272", "ch": 32, "n": 6, "title": "Tricuspid Atresia", "sec": "Tricuspid atresia · p144–145", "qs": ["PEDS-C32-065", "PEDS-C32-066", "PEDS-C32-067", "PEDS-C32-068", "PEDS-C32-069", "PEDS-C32-070", "PEDS-C32-071", "PEDS-C32-072", "PEDS-C32-073", "PEDS-C32-074", "PEDS-C32-075"], "guide": "Atresia of tricuspid valve → ↓ blood flow to RV → ↓ blood flow to PA → cyanosis. PFO or ASD mandatory → overload of blood to LA and LV → hypertrophy of left heart. ECG: left-axis deviation. Note: all CHD are diagnosed by ECHO cardiography. Treatment: staged shunt surgery — 1. modified B-T shunt (immediately) → 2. Glenn shunt (SVC to PA) → 3. Fontan shunt (IVC to PA)."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U273", "ch": 32, "n": 7, "title": "Ebstein's Anomaly", "sec": "Ebstein's anomaly · p145–146", "qs": ["PEDS-C32-076", "PEDS-C32-077", "PEDS-C32-078", "PEDS-C32-079", "PEDS-C32-080", "PEDS-C32-081", "PEDS-C32-082", "PEDS-C32-083", "PEDS-C32-084", "PEDS-C32-085", "PEDS-C32-086", "PEDS-C32-087", "PEDS-C32-088", "PEDS-C32-089", "PEDS-C32-090"], "guide": "Inferior/apical displacement of septal leaflet of tricuspid valve (normal position shown) → atrialization of RV; ↑ RA size; ↓ RV size → ↓ RV blood volume → ↓ blood flow to PA → cyanosis. X-ray: box-shaped heart (increased PA size). Associations: lithium exposure; accessory pathways on right side — WPW (Bundle of Kent: RA→RV) → early pre-excitation of RV → slurred QRS (delta wave, short PR, wide QRS). Treatment: cone repair of tricuspid valve, return valve to original position."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U274", "ch": 32, "n": 8, "title": "Hypoplastic Left Heart Syndrome (HLHS)", "sec": "HLHS · p146", "qs": ["PEDS-C32-091", "PEDS-C32-092", "PEDS-C32-093", "PEDS-C32-094", "PEDS-C32-095", "PEDS-C32-096", "PEDS-C32-097", "PEDS-C32-098", "PEDS-C32-099", "PEDS-C32-100", "PEDS-C32-101"], "guide": "1. atresia of mitral valve → no communication between LA and LV; 2. hypoplastic LV; 3. hypoplastic aorta → severely ↓ systemic flow → shock in neonates. ASD seen in majority of cases → ↑ blood flow to RA & RV → early onset CCF (< 1 week). Treatment: fatal if untreated/delayed; Norwood procedure — surgical creation of Neo (new) aorta to ↑ blood flow."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U275", "ch": 32, "n": 9, "title": "Truncus Arteriosus", "sec": "Truncus arteriosus · p146–147", "qs": ["PEDS-C32-102", "PEDS-C32-103", "PEDS-C32-104", "PEDS-C32-105", "PEDS-C32-106", "PEDS-C32-107", "PEDS-C32-108", "PEDS-C32-109"], "guide": "Common outflow tract (TA) — mixing of oxygenated and deoxygenated blood from RV and LV → cyanosis. A type of conotruncal defect (includes TOF, interrupted aortic arch etc.); associated with DiGeorge syndrome. Treatment: Rastelli's procedure — truncus arteriosus partitioned → normal blood outflow."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U276", "ch": 32, "n": 10, "title": "Transposition of Great Arteries (TGA)", "sec": "TGA · p147", "qs": ["PEDS-C32-110", "PEDS-C32-111", "PEDS-C32-112", "PEDS-C32-113", "PEDS-C32-114", "PEDS-C32-115", "PEDS-C32-116", "PEDS-C32-117", "PEDS-C32-118", "PEDS-C32-119", "PEDS-C32-120", "PEDS-C32-121", "PEDS-C32-122", "PEDS-C32-123", "PEDS-C32-124", "PEDS-C32-125", "PEDS-C32-126"], "guide": "TGA with intact ventricular septum: parallel circulation (separate tracts for oxygenated and deoxygenated blood) → early onset cyanosis (within few minutes) → fatal. TGA with VSD: blood flows LV→RV, mixing → less intense cyanosis + pansystolic murmur + CCF. X-ray: egg (heart) + string (narrow positioning of great arteries) = egg-on-string appearance. Treatment (intact septum): emergency — 1. PGE-1 infusion immediately at birth (keeps DA open: O2 blood PA→aorta); 2. atrial septostomy (RA↔LA connection → ↑ O2 status); definitive: Jatene's arterial switch repair. TGA with VSD: electively (few weeks after birth) → Jatene's."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U277", "ch": 32, "n": 11, "title": "Total Anomalous Pulmonary Venous Connections (TAPVC)", "sec": "TAPVC · p148", "qs": ["PEDS-C32-127", "PEDS-C32-128", "PEDS-C32-129", "PEDS-C32-130", "PEDS-C32-131", "PEDS-C32-132", "PEDS-C32-133", "PEDS-C32-134", "PEDS-C32-135", "PEDS-C32-136", "PEDS-C32-137", "PEDS-C32-138", "PEDS-C32-139", "PEDS-C32-140", "PEDS-C32-141", "PEDS-C32-142", "PEDS-C32-143"], "guide": "Abnormal connections between PV and RA. Types by route: 1. supracardiac (m/c) — PV → superior vena cava → RA; 2. cardiac — PV → RA directly; 3. infracardiac — PV → portal veins → RA. Obstructive type: pulmonary venous obstruction → congestion of lungs → severe cyanosis. Non-obstructive (m/c): equal O2 saturation in all heart chambers; ASD with wide fixed splitting of S2; mixed blood in aorta → cyanosis. X-ray: supracardiac TAPVC — snowman/figure-of-8 appearance (d/t ↑ SVC size)."},
